// test-error
// test-adr: 045
// test-transpile-only
// Issue #1361: this `.expected.error` existed with no `.test.cnx` beside it, so
// it could never run -- while still occupying a row in
// `docs/diagnostic-manifest.md` and appearing, in #1321's audit, to cover the
// `Array size mismatch` throws in `StringDeclHelper` and `ArrayInitHelper`.
// Coverage that cannot execute is worse than none: it reads as green.

// NEGATIVE CONTROL -- declared first, and must stay silent.
// A check that compared the wrong pair, or fired on any string array with an
// initializer, would reject this one too. Because a throw aborts at the first
// occurrence, over-enforcement here changes the reported message rather than
// adding a line, so the exact-match assertion in the .expected.error catches it.
const string<8>[3] EXACT <- ["One", "Two", "Three"];

// THE ASSERTION -- declared [3], given 2.
// NEGATIVE CONTROL -- the same declaration with the right number of elements.
// `EXACT` is already here and must stay silent; the rule counts, so a check
// that rejected every list would fail on it.
const string<8>[3] SHORT <- ["One", "Two"];
